What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/.../dram/type
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Description:
                Read-only DRAM family, currently "lpddr5". This family
                includes LPDDR5X; the attribute does not assert the X suffix.
                The dram group is present on an apple-pmp-report device only
                when DT supplies a complete, consistent memory description,
                or on T6000, T8112, T6040 and T8140 with an older boot DT.
                The latter uses the same static interface class as the DTS,
                selected by both root SoC and PMP report compatibles. Other
                SoCs do not inherit a class from a shared PMP layout. Complete
                DT metadata takes precedence; invalid metadata is rejected.
                Static attributes remain valid when firmware is stopped.
                Typical paths are:
                /sys/bus/platform/devices/3003c0000.pmp-report/dram/ (T8140)
                /sys/bus/platform/devices/5003c0000.pmp-report/dram/ (T6040).
                There is no dram devfreq class device. These files require
                CONFIG_APPLE_PMP_REPORT and its bound pmp_report driver, not
                CONFIG_APPLE_PMP_DRAM_KUNIT_TEST (which only enables tests).
                Installing kernel DTBs alone does not refresh a live DT
                supplied by an older Stage 2 bootloader.

What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/.../dram/max_data_rate
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Description:
                Read-only maximum interface transfers per second per data pin
                (divide by 1000000 for MT/s), from the highest DT OPP or the
                compatible-selected static interface class on an older DT. This is
                an inferred interface class, not a measured current rate or
                a literal LPDDR5 command clock/WCK. The maximum state ID is
                state_count minus one, independent of DT child order.

What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/.../dram/peak_bandwidth
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Description:
                Read-only inferred physical maximum in decimal bytes/second,
                max_data_rate * data_bus_width / 8. This excludes ECC/check bits
                and does not measure sustainable application bandwidth.

What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/.../dram/bandwidth_class
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Description:
                Read-only published maximum bandwidth class in decimal
                bytes/second. It may be rounded relative to peak_bandwidth.

What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/.../dram/data_bus_width
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Description:
                Read-only inferred usable data width in bits, excluding ECC.

What:           /sys/bus/platform/devices/.../dram/state_count
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Description:
                Read-only number of firmware DCS states, from DT or the
                compatible-selected static interface class on an older DT. State IDs
                are not frequencies. No current-state, current-rate, residency,
                or transition-statistics attribute is provided without an
                independently specified achieved-state transport.
